	 show-layer-names="false" show-layer-rects="false">
<database name="e7gz_ps" encoding="UTF8" is-template="false" allow-conns="true">
	<role name="postgres"/>
	<tablespace name="pg_default"/>
	<comment> <![CDATA[ Authority: Product Specification v5.0 FROZEN > PRD v1.1 APPROVED > FRS v1.1 APPROVED > Approved Product Clarification TRUST-001 > Product Clarification LOY-001 (adopted 25 Sep 2026, historical Points reward anchor) > Technical Architecture v1.2 FROZEN BUILD BASELINE > this database model. A1: overlapping/back-to-back Maintenance on same Resource is allowed. A2: 120-day rolling Operating Session materialization is accepted as an Architecture setting, not Product behaviour. pgModeler 1.2.2 compatibility: identity login fields are modeled as PostgreSQL text; normalized case-insensitive uniqueness is enforced by functional unique indexes in this model, so no Product behavior is changed and no citext type dependency is required for model loading. Inventory + Operations + Booking + Attendance + Tournament hardened delivery requires the paired Flyway generic-guard migrations and deployment-security SQL; production DDL must carry p0_p1_hardening_guards, v1_1_5_integrity_guards, v1_1_6_operations_hardening_guards, v1_1_7_booking_hardening_guards, v1_1_8_booking_acceptance_guards, v1_1_9_attendance_hardening_guards, v1_1_10_attendance_acceptance_guards, v1_1_11_tournament_hardening_guards, v1_1_12_tournament_acceptance_guards and v1_1_13_tournament_final_acceptance_guards, v1_1_16_tournament_final_source_baseline_guards, v1_1_17_tournament_participant_cause_finalized_guards, v1_1_18_trust_hardening_guards, v1_1_19_trust_acceptance_corrections and v1_1_20_trust_replay_ban_exact_set_corrections and v1_1_21_trust_shared_command_reconciliation and v1_1_22_trust_focused_acceptance_corrections. The deployment-security SQL defines the implementation-only e7gz_app_runtime database role and controlled immutable/one-time-close privileges, not Product RBAC.  v1.1.23 adds Loyalty source-bound ledgers/refund settlement and owner-validated Admin command contexts. Run the v1.1.23 security companion after export. v1.1.24 adds v1_1_24_loyalty_anchor_refund_corrections: LOY-001 immutable original reward anchor (AR23-01), explicit Admin service-loss assessment separating the fee decision from positive refund entitlement (AR23-02), and the Loyalty write_guard execution fix (AR24-X01); run the v1.1.24 security delta after the v1.1.23 companion. v1.1.25 adds v1_1_25_platform_hardening (Reviews, Notifications, Configuration, Idempotency, Outbox, Scheduler, shared trusted Admin command context, Audit provenance/redaction/append-only, Admin Alerts) with native constraints/indexes; run the v1.1.25 security delta after the v1.1.24 delta. v1.1.26 incorporates PCR-001..003 at the database boundary: exact Tournament participant causes, Customer Account Deletion requests, and Customer Review reports. Apply the v1.1.26 security delta after v1.1.25. v1.1.27 (v1_1_27_review_fixes) corrects review findings against Product v5.0 / FRS v1.1: Player-hosted Tournament approval window MIN(created+10 min, checkpoint), startAt-2h cutoff for both host types, REJECTED carries VENUE_REJECTED_TOURNAMENT and approval timeout is CANCELLED/VENUE_DID_NOT_APPROVE_TOURNAMENT_IN_TIME (FR-TRN-10); Ban ending exactly at startAt no longer restores; O19 anonymisation producer removes deleted-account Reviews and completes the deletion request; Global Booking Fee and Tournament Creation Fee are versioned configuration; username cooldown, Area, OTP, Online intake and Operating Session history guards; user_commitment_guard auto-created; SECURITY DEFINER functions revoked from PUBLIC; FK indexes. Apply the v1.1.27 security delta after v1.1.26. Runtime DDL + targeted behaviour tests were executed on PostgreSQL 16 for v1.1.27 (see change report).]]> </comment>
</database>

