<textbox name="00_Authority_and_Freeze" layers="0" z-value="0" width="1676.86" font-size="10">
	<position x="200" y="20"/>
	<comment> <![CDATA[E7GZ PS — DATABASE MODEL v1.1.21 — TRUST SHARED-COMMAND CORRECTED / REVIEW CANDIDATE
Authority: Product Spec v5.0 > PRD v1.1 > FRS v1.1 > Technical Architecture v1.2 FROZEN BUILD BASELINE > DB Model.
A1 CLOSED: Maintenance windows on the same Resource may overlap/back-to-back; overlap must not be double-counted in rolling maintenance time.
A2 CLOSED: 120-day rolling Operating Session materialization is accepted as Architecture only, not as a Product booking limit.
Critical: Venue row + Resource row + user_commitment_guard serialize commitment/cascade races. Booking NO_SHOW is terminal with NULL Booking Reason Code; its separate domains are status NO_SHOW, event NO_SHOW_RECORDED and Attendance Result ABSENT_NO_SHOW. Deployment: carry p0_p1_hardening_guards, v1_1_5_integrity_guards, v1_1_6_operations_hardening_guards, v1_1_7_booking_hardening_guards, v1_1_8_booking_acceptance_guards, v1_1_9_attendance_hardening_guards, v1_1_10_attendance_acceptance_guards, v1_1_11_tournament_hardening_guards, v1_1_12_tournament_acceptance_guards and v1_1_13_tournament_final_acceptance_guards into Flyway/production DDL; use the v1.1.13 deployment-security SQL so immutable stores and controlled Tournament/Attendance lifecycle updates remain physically enforced.]]> </comment>
</textbox>

