<textbox name="inventory_critical_invariants" layers="0" z-value="0" width="1709.28" font-size="9">
	<position x="5400" y="4000"/>
	<comment> <![CDATA[CRITICAL DATABASE INVARIANTS
I1 Resource double-booking: GiST exclusion for exclusive commitment ranges + transactional cross-class conflict guard. MAINTENANCE↔MAINTENANCE is allowed.
I2 Customer schedule overlap: exclusion on counted ONLINE commitment_period; max-4 enforced while holding iam.user_commitment_guard.
I3 Operating Sessions: non-overlap by Venue; 24h maximum is local template rule, not absolute duration.
I4 Booking terminal semantics: REJECTED/CANCELLED require exactly one closed Booking Reason Code; COMPLETED/NO_SHOW have NULL Booking Reason Code. NO_SHOW_RECORDED and ABSENT_NO_SHOW remain separate Event/Attendance domains. Tournament COMPLETED has NULL reason.
I5 Trust: immutable event stream ordered effective_at,event_sequence; corrections reference original + superseded correction explicitly.
I6 Security rate limits: Redis may accelerate but PostgreSQL fallback/fail-closed is authoritative.
I7 Booking history is append-only; historical Booking identity/configuration/money/session snapshots cannot be silently rewritten; Late Confirmation must own exactly one canonical LATE_CONFIRM_HOLD while open, and open/closed state is represented by technical closed_at rather than inferred from Customer response.]]> </comment>
</textbox>

<textbox name="inventory_operations_booking_delivery_gate" layers="0" z-value="0" width="2094.7" font-size="9">
	<position x="8000" y="4000"/>
	<comment> <![CDATA[INVENTORY + OPERATIONS + BOOKING + ATTENDANCE + TOURNAMENT DELIVERY GATE — v1.1.13
1) PostgreSQL Generic SQL blocks are executable baseline requirements. Production Flyway must carry p0_p1_hardening_guards, v1_1_5_integrity_guards, v1_1_6_operations_hardening_guards, v1_1_7_booking_hardening_guards, v1_1_8_booking_acceptance_guards, v1_1_9_attendance_hardening_guards, v1_1_10_attendance_acceptance_guards, v1_1_11_tournament_hardening_guards, v1_1_12_tournament_acceptance_guards and v1_1_13_tournament_final_acceptance_guards.
2) Use the v1.1.11 deployment-security SQL for e7gz_app_runtime: append-only history/audit stays SELECT/INSERT-only; Tournament aggregate, Resource and Participant tables receive only approved lifecycle-column UPDATE rights.
3) Tournament creation is atomic with 1–4 Resource Holds, state history, durable approval/checkpoint/start/end jobs and outbox. Player-hosted creation locks the creator and enforces Verified/not-banned/one-pending/cooldown rules; resource commitment paths follow creator/venue/resource/tournament lock order.
4) Venue Accept physically releases immutable TOURNAMENT_APPROVAL_HOLD rows and inserts TOURNAMENT_HOLD rows, updating tournament_resource.reservation_id once; historical Hold rows are never rewritten. Checkpoint/start commands revalidate operational eligibility and participant count under locks.
5) Attendance/Booking rules from v1.1.10 remain mandatory. Deadline ownership is authoritative: now < deadline may act; now >= deadline belongs to the scheduled boundary. Subsequent module hardening must extend this checkpoint rather than weaken earlier guards.]]> </comment>
</textbox>

<table name="user_account" layers="0" collapse-mode="2" max-obj-count="16" z-value="0">
	<schema name="iam"/>
	<role name="postgres"/>
	<comment> <![CDATA[Anonymisation blanks PII but keeps the id, so every historical reference survives.

Source/critical constraints:
- ux_user_username (WHERE anonymised_at IS NULL)
- ux_user_phone

pgModeler-native representation: username and email are stored as text. Username comparison remains trimmed + case-insensitive through ux_user_username_normalized; customer email is not unique. Anonymisation preserves immutable User ID.]]> </comment>
	<position x="200" y="480"/>
	<column name="id" not-null="true">
		<type name="uuid" length="0"/>
	</column>
	<column name="full_name" not-null="true">
		<type name="text" length="0"/>
		<comment> <![CDATA[freely editable — FR-ACC-07]]> </comment>
	</column>
	<column name="username" not-null="true">
		<type name="text" length="0"/>
		<comment> <![CDATA[normalised trimmed + case-insensitive — FR-ACC-06]]> </comment>
	</column>
	<column name="phone_e164" not-null="true">
		<type name="text" length="0"/>
		<comment> <![CDATA[FR-ACC-01]]> </comment>
	</column>
	<column name="email" not-null="true">
		<type name="text" length="0"/>
		<comment> <![CDATA[not unique — FR-ACC-01]]> </comment>
	</column>
	<column name="password_hash" not-null="true">
		<type name="text" length="0"/>
		<comment> <![CDATA[Argon2id]]> </comment>
	</column>
	<column name="phone_verified" not-null="true">
		<type name="boolean" length="0"/>
		<comment> <![CDATA[THE marketplace activation gate — FR-ACC-02]]> </comment>
	</column>
	<column name="phone_verified_at">
		<type name="timestamp with time zone" length="0" with-timezone="true"/>
	</column>
	<column name="email_verified" not-null="true">
		<type name="boolean" length="0"/>
		<comment> <![CDATA[never activates — FR-ACC-02]]> </comment>
	</column>
	<column name="referral_code" not-null="true">
		<type name="text" length="0"/>
	</column>
	<column name="referred_by_code">
		<type name="text" length="0"/>
		<comment> <![CDATA[FR-PTS-06]]> </comment>
	</column>
	<column name="anonymised_at">
		<type name="timestamp with time zone" length="0" with-timezone="true"/>
		<comment> <![CDATA[completed deletion/anonymisation path — FR-ACC-10 / PCR-002]]> </comment>
	</column>
	<column name="joined_at" not-null="true">
		<type name="timestamp with time zone" length="0" with-timezone="true"/>
	</column>
	<constraint name="user_account_pk" type="pk-constr" table="iam.user_account">
		<columns names="id" ref-type="src-columns"/>
	</constraint>
	<constraint name="uq_user_account_phone_e164" type="uq-constr" table="iam.user_account">
		<columns names="phone_e164" ref-type="src-columns"/>
	</constraint>
	<constraint name="uq_user_account_referral_code" type="uq-constr" table="iam.user_account">
		<columns names="referral_code" ref-type="src-columns"/>
	</constraint>
	<constraint name="ck_user_phone_verification" type="ck-constr" table="iam.user_account">
			<expression> <![CDATA[phone_verified = (phone_verified_at IS NOT NULL)]]> </expression>
	</constraint>
	<constraint name="ck_user_anonymised_pii" type="ck-constr" table="iam.user_account">
			<expression> <![CDATA[anonymised_at IS NULL OR (full_name = '' AND email = '' AND password_hash = '' AND phone_e164 = 'anonymised:' || id::text)]]> </expression>
	</constraint>
</table>

<table name="venue_account" layers="0" collapse-mode="2" max-obj-count="7" z-value="0">
	<schema name="iam"/>
	<role name="postgres"/>
	<comment> <![CDATA[One shared Venue Account per Venue. login_identifier is text in the visual model; ux_venue_login_normalized enforces trimmed case-insensitive uniqueness. Owner Password is stored separately.]]> </comment>
	<position x="200" y="1520"/>
	<column name="id" not-null="true">
		<type name="uuid" length="0"/>
	</column>
	<column name="venue_id" not-null="true">
		<type name="uuid" length="0"/>
		<comment> <![CDATA[UNIQUE — one shared account per venue, FR-VEN-01]]> </comment>
	</column>
	<column name="login_identifier" not-null="true">
		<type name="text" length="0"/>
	</column>
	<column name="password_hash" not-null="true">
		<type name="text" length="0"/>
		<comment> <![CDATA[Argon2id]]> </comment>
	</column>
	<column name="account_status" not-null="true">
		<type name="varchar" length="80"/>
		<comment> <![CDATA[ENABLED · DISABLED]]> </comment>
	</column>
	<column name="language_preference" not-null="true">
		<type name="text" length="0"/>
		<comment> <![CDATA[en | ar — FR-VEN-40]]> </comment>
	</column>
	<constraint name="venue_account_pk" type="pk-constr" table="iam.venue_account">
		<columns names="id" ref-type="src-columns"/>
